  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1238 AM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nAnother hot day is expected on Tuesday with the potential for \nanother Heat Advisory for Fremont, Pueblo, and El Paso County, \nhowever the temperatures decrease a few degrees so the eastern \nplains should not be included. Heights rise a little on Tuesday, \nwhich brings a slight drying prior to widespread mountain rainfall \non Wednesday. The storms that do develop will still primarily be \ngusty outflow producers with winds up to 50 MPH under the strongest \nstorms. \n\nWednesday will be hot once again, but closer to seasonal, so no Heat \nAdvisories are expected. However, data is trending towards heavy \nrainfall over the mountains, which raises concerns for flash \nflooding over the Aspen Acres and 24 burn scars. This trend will \ncontinue throughout the rest of the forecast period and even into \nnext week. With the widespread rainfall temperatures will be below \naverage for this time of year. Flash flooding will be an issue over \nthe burn scars, urban corridors, and areas with saturated soils.",
